selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.contour_corner_knots\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.contour_corner_knots\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">contour_corner_knots</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">contour</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">grid</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">tolerance</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.001</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Interior grid positions where the meridian\u2019s tangent jumps.</p><p>The throat carries independent slopes on either side, and interpolated\ncontours corner at every input point. A spline may only be fitted through\na smooth run, so these are the positions the run has to be cut at.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"PlanarLine.html#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.PlanarLine\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.PlanarLine\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PlanarLine</span></span></dt><dd><p>Directed line, sharing the sampling/export contract of PlanarArc.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"TangentBezier.html#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.TangentBezier\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.TangentBezier\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">TangentBezier</span></span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._station_index\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._station_index\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_station_index</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">stations</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">x</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Index of the construction sample at <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">x</span></code>.</p><p>Every hot-wall station is one of the samples its channel was constructed\non, so this is an exact lookup. Silently taking a neighbouring station\u2019s\ngeometry would mis-place the arc, so an inexact match is an error.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Geometry-only transverse sections and hot-wall surfaces.</p><p>No solver dimensions, paths or section analytics are modified here. Oblique\nsections represent the local prismatic approximation, not exact CAD sweep cuts.</p>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.transverse_matrix\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.transverse_matrix\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">transverse_matrix</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">construction</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">planes</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">index</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"#functions\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Functions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#functions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.hot_wall_regions\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.hot_wall_regions\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">hot_wall_regions</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">spans</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">squared</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">contour_span</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transition_fraction</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.02</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Partition covered spans by construction type and active channel seeds.</p><p>With rounded channels, changes into/out of shared spans leave a centered\nopen transition zone. Its width is a fraction of the full contour length,\nmatching the former blend-zone convention. Empty spans are never connected.\nSquared-only spans can share a revolve regardless of channel count or winding.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"PlanarArc.html#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.PlanarArc\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.PlanarArc\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PlanarArc</span></span></dt><dd><p>Affine circular arc: c + a*cos(t) + b*sin(t), in metres.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._interval_bezier\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._interval_bezier\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_interval_bezier</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">contour</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">a</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">b</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>The cubic Bezier through four evenly spaced samples of one interval.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._hot_arc\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._hot_arc\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_hot_arc</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">construction</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transverse</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">index</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.join_hot_wall\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.join_hot_wall\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">join_hot_wall</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">pieces</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">trim_fraction</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Join angularly ordered (id, type, arc, reference angle) pieces.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#classes\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Classes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#classes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.transverse_construction\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.transverse_construction\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">transverse_construction</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">construction</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._secant_tangent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._secant_tangent\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_secant_tangent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">contour</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">x</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">step</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Unit (radius, axial) tangent of the meridian, from a short secant.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">step</span></code> is signed: a negative step reads the interval behind <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">x</span></code>. The\nresult always points in the direction of increasing axial position, so a\ncontour corner shows up as two differing tangents at one knot.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._span_union\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._span_union\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_span_union</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">spans</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._rotation\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry._rotation\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_rotation</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">angle</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"#module-contents\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Module Contents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-contents\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.build_hot_wall\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.build_hot_wall\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">build_hot_wall</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">chamber</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">resolved</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">trim_fraction</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.1</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transition_fraction</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.02</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Export contour revolves and independent, circumferentially blended lofts.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"TransverseConstruction.html#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.TransverseConstruction\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.TransverseConstruction\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">TransverseConstruction</span></span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.hot_wall_revolve\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.hot_wall_revolve\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cad_geometry.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">hot_wall_revolve</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">contour</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">start</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">end</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Meridional splines in (radius, axial) mm, one per smooth contour run.</p><p>Each spline interpolates the contour\u2019s own knots, so CAD receives one\ncurve where the contour is smooth instead of a chain of short segments\nthat reads as faceted. Runs are cut at tangent discontinuities, which\nkeeps the throat corner sharp, and a trimmed span contributes its exact\nendpoints without depending on coolant sampling.</p></dd>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
